9	 * reports `Should not import the named export 'version' … from default-exporting
10	 * module` at the module-graph layer, after the program has compiled. The two
11	 * layers disagree, and the era's builder never surfaced the disagreement because
12	 * its loader synthesised the named bindings.
13	 *
14	 * The successor shape is not a choice. A JSON module has exactly one export
15	 * shape, so the named binding is a property of the default export and nothing
16	 * else: take the default, then bind the same names off it. The rewrite therefore
17	 * touches the import declaration and adds one destructuring statement beside it,
18	 * and every use site in the file keeps the identifier it already had.
19	 *
